# Cron schedule for the `scheduler` docker-compose service (see
# nas/scheduler_entrypoint.sh and NAS_SETUP.md, "Schedule the recurring
# jobs"). Installed into /etc/cron.d/ at container startup by the
# entrypoint script -- editing this file requires a `docker-compose build`
# + `docker-compose up -d scheduler` to take effect, same as any other
# code change.
#
# NOT a `TZ=` line here: that was tried first and confirmed broken by a
# live run that fired at 16:30 UTC (12:30pm ET) instead of 16:30 ET. A
# `TZ=` assignment inside a cron.d file is only exported into each job's
# OWN environment -- it does not change what wall-clock time the cron
# DAEMON itself uses to evaluate the schedule below. The daemon's own
# clock follows the container's own environment, so the timezone is set
# via `environment: - TZ=America/New_York` on the `scheduler` service in
# docker-compose.yml instead (see the comment there) -- that's what
# actually makes "30 16 * * 1-5" below mean 4:30pm America/New_York, DST
# included, not a fixed UTC offset that drifts twice a year.
#
# PATH= IS a real, working cron.d directive (unlike TZ=) -- explicit here
# because cron's own default PATH is a bare `/usr/bin:/bin`, which does
# NOT include /usr/local/bin, where the official python Docker image
# actually installs `python`/`python3`. Confirmed live: the very first
# scheduled run failed with "python: command not found" before this line
# was added, even though python is definitely on the image -- cron's
# minimal default PATH just couldn't see it.
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin

# /etc/cron.d files require a user field (root) that a personal crontab
# (`crontab -e`) does not -- don't drop it if you copy these lines
# elsewhere. Each job explicitly invokes `bash -c '...'` (not cron's
# default /bin/sh) because /etc/environment below is written with bash's
# `%q` quoting (see scheduler_entrypoint.sh) -- sourcing it under a
# POSIX /bin/sh (dash on this image) can misparse that quoting.

# Daily Ingest + Compute -- weekdays, 4:30pm ET (30 min after US market
# close, same buffer the old GitHub Actions cron used).
30 16 * * 1-5 root bash -c '. /etc/environment && cd /app && bash nas/daily_pipeline.sh' >> /app/logs/cron.log 2>&1

# Weekly Universe Refresh -- Saturdays at 6am ET (markets closed, no
# urgency, just needs to run sometime before Monday's daily pipeline).
0 6 * * 6 root bash -c '. /etc/environment && cd /app && bash nas/weekly_refresh.sh' >> /app/logs/cron.log 2>&1

# Cron requires a trailing blank line -- don't remove it.
